WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.586
The first fictional offer promises higher income and business success from a planning template.

00:00:06.586 --> 00:00:08.938
That guarantee is not supported.

00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:15.994
Organize the Responsible Offer Frame: audience, need, value, content or service, format, responsibility and limits.

00:00:15.994 --> 00:00:19.757
Name the small-business owner and weekly planning task.

00:00:19.757 --> 00:00:23.520
State the actual template, instructions, example and checklist.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.695
Explain the useful action: organizing priorities, task owners and review questions.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:32.458
State what the user must supply and check.

00:00:32.458 --> 00:00:36.692
Exclude personalized advice and outcomes outside the provider’s control.

00:00:36.692 --> 00:00:39.985
An offer describes the promise and exchange.

00:00:39.985 --> 00:00:42.337
The template is the product.

00:00:42.337 --> 00:00:49.863
A personal review would be a service, and receiving and using the resource involves delivery activities.

00:00:49.863 --> 00:00:53.156
Correct the guarantee in the offer itself.

00:00:53.156 --> 00:00:58.801
Adding a small disclaimer while keeping the claim does not fix it.
